A||||4||theogre||HOW TO: Adding lower courtesy lights under dash.||||4||
Z||000000||theogre||05-14-2000||12:46 PM||||When I stripped the dash out of another car I was able to get the actual harness addon to add the low mount courtesy lights. Man what a diferance to interior lighting.<P>There are 2 ways to add this. ((NO, I don't know if it's the same for the 84's.))<P>1. Obviously, you can locate the harness addon. It's a simple matter of plugging it into the factory harness. The connector and brackets for it are installed in all cars wether they have the option or not. Problem is you have to rip out the whole dash to get this addon out of the car.<P>2. MAke the harness addon.<P>This actually isn't hard. You need 4 crimp on but splices and 2 wire taps. (Those things where you squash the mettal tab into the wires and flip the little lid over to close it.) you also need about 10 feet of 18-20ga lamp cord and 2 marker light sockets. (I'll look up a good one at the parts store next time I go so you can buy new ones.)<P>The marker light sockets you want are a bit hard to describe. They are rubber and use 2 or 4 ears to lock into a hole. They hold the same type lamp as Fiero side markers. (Fiero marker sockets won't work.)<P>To start remove the Courtesy lamp fuse. This circuit is hot at all times.<P>connect 2 peices of lamp cord to one light socket with but splices. One wire should be long enough to reach the left speaker. the other goes across the car to the other socket.<P>The bracket for the left light is on the right side of the fuse box. It's that hole with 4 little ears in it. The socket goes in from the top so the lamp sticks out the bottom.<P>Take out the left speaker. Thread the short wire up to the black connector under the speaker that has white and orange wires on it. (connector color may vary the wire won't)<P>use the taps to connect the lamp cord to these wires. You don't have to strip the wires to use the taps. polarity doesn't matter.<P>thread the long lamp cord across the car to the right bracket located at the lower <BR>corner of the dash. connect the last socket to the wire and put the socket in the bracket.<P>put lamps in both sockets and your done.<P>put the fuse back in and the lamps should come right on.<P>the whole project should only take about 30-40 minutes max.||||reg||4
Z||000001||Rodrv6||05-14-2000||01:49 PM||||Ogre,<BR>The 84's are the same.  I've done mine and I can't find any difference between what you say to do and what I did.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
